{#
  Version 3's front door: an unauthenticated page explaining what the service
  is, prompting the reader to sign in. Replaces v2's split between "Find and
  locate guidance" and "Manage all guidance documents" — in v3 there is one
  way in, and the signed-in landing page (search.html) does the rest.

  The full-bleed green hero and its white start button follow the Defra AI
  toolkit's (digital.defra.gov.uk/ai-toolkit) — see .app-v3-hero in
  app/assets/sass/components/_app-v3.scss, which notes which of its classes
  each piece came from. The bordered "What you can do" panel is that hero's
  "what's new" box, repurposed.

  Signing in is as fake as everywhere else in this prototype — the one
  real thing it now records is a role (see app/data/context-pane.js), used
  to vary the context pane's content between an expert reader and a
  designer/author. The question sits in the plain white section below the
  hero (govuk-radios directly on the green hero's own dark background would
  be a contrast problem — GOV.UK's default label/border colours assume a
  light background), but is inside the same <form> as the hero's own
  button, so submitting it still reads as one step, not two.
#}
{% extends "layouts/v3.html" %}

{% from "govuk/components/button/macro.njk" import govukButton %}
{% from "govuk/components/inset-text/macro.njk" import govukInsetText %}
{% from "govuk/components/phase-banner/macro.njk" import govukPhaseBanner %}
{% from "govuk/components/radios/macro.njk" import govukRadios %}

{% set pageName = "Sign in" %}

{#
  The phase banner normally renders in beforeContent, above everything — but
  a band of banner between the header and the hero broke the full-bleed
  green, so this page suppresses it there and re-renders it under the hero
  instead.
#}
{% block beforeContent %}{% endblock %}

{% block content %}

<form method="post" action="/2026-09-29-sidenav-first-prototype/sign-in">

<div class="app-v3-hero">
  <div class="app-v3-hero__inner">

    <div class="app-v3-hero__content">
      {# The caption carries "Rural Payments Agency", so the title drops the
         RPA prefix from serviceName rather than repeating it. #}
      <p class="app-v3-hero__caption">Rural Payments Agency</p>
      <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl app-v3-hero__title">Guidance Hub</h1>
      <p class="govuk-body-l app-v3-hero__description">
        Find, review and manage RPA guidance documents, all in one place.
      </p>

      {{ govukButton({
        text: "Sign in",
        type: "submit",
        isStartButton: true,
        classes: "app-v3-hero__start-button"
      }) }}

      <p class="govuk-body app-v3-hero__note">
        This is an internal service. You need a Defra account to sign in.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="app-v3-hero__panel">
      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">What you can do in the hub</h2>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>search all RPA guidance by document name, scheme or topic</li>
        <li>check whether a document is up to date</li>
        <li>pick up drafts you are working on</li>
        <li>review and approve documents sent to you</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </div>
</div>

{{ govukPhaseBanner({
  tag: { text: "Prototype" },
  text: "This is a prototype for user research. Nothing you enter is saved."
}) }}

<div class="app-v3-prose govuk-!-margin-top-6">

  {{ govukRadios({
    idPrefix: "role",
    name: "role",
    fieldset: {
      legend: { text: "Sign in as", classes: "govuk-fieldset__legend--m" }
    },
    hint: { text: "This decides what the guidance hub's context pane shows you — you can switch at any time from there." },
    items: [
      { value: "viewer", text: "Viewer — search for and read guidance", checked: selectedRole == "viewer" },
      { value: "designer", text: "Designer — author and manage guidance", checked: selectedRole == "designer" }
    ]
  }) }}

  {{ govukInsetText({
    text: "This prototype does not sign you in. Selecting the button takes you to the guidance hub."
  }) }}

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">If you cannot sign in</h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Email the AI Capability and Enablement team at
    <a class="govuk-link" href="mailto:AICapabilityAndEnablement@defra.gov.uk">AICapabilityAndEnablement@defra.gov.uk</a>.
  </p>

</div>

</form>

{% endblock %}
